            <ArticleTitle>Utilizing an oral sucrose solution to minimize neonatal pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="ISSUES AND PURPOSE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To present an evidence-based practice protocol for oral sucrose administration to minimize neonatal procedural pain.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Examination of published research may provide additional modalities to expand an established pediatric pain-management program.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="PRACTICAL IMPLICATIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The extensive research evaluating oral sucrose supports its inclusion in a pediatric pain-management program. A thorough implementation plan will allow new modalities to be included to optimize procedural pain relief for hospitalized neonates with minimal staff resistance and improved patient outcomes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
